A||||12||fiero56||"notchy" shifting||||1||
Z||000000||fiero56||02-14-2000||09:24 PM||||I have an '88 Formula(v-6, 5-speed). When shifting from one gear to the next there is "catch". Like when you grind a gear, but only over one tooth spinning slowly. It is felt in the shifter as the shifter is engaging the next higher gear(1 to 2 especially, 3 to 4 a little bit, 4 to 5 no catch). I don't notice it when downshifting, only when upshifting. The "catch" only happens when going into the next gear, not when leaving the gear currently selected. <BR>I asked this question several months ago. Was told to try replacing tranny fluid(didn't help), adjusted shift linkage(didn't help). New clutch(didn't expect it to help and it didn't).<BR>I notice this catch gets less severe the longer the engine is running/car is driven. After 15 to 20 minutes(winter), 5 to 10 minutes(summer) it is no longer there. My only guess is as the tranny fluid warms it becomes thinner, allowing something in the tranny to operate properly again.<BR>At least one other person has told me they have this same problem. What causes it? Bad syncros?||||reg||1
Z||000001||stimpy||02-14-2000||10:06 PM||||I have this problem on my Mazda 323 GTX. I inquired on the 323 webring and was told that bad syncros were the culprit. Apparently that tranny (4wd 5spd) is notorious for that. Still a lot of fun in the snow and mud! I think I saw some threads sayin that Fiero 5spd is weak in the 3rd gear syncro. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Shiner||02-14-2000||10:21 PM||||I can verify that the 3rd gear synchro is weak on 5speeds.  Mine is pretty far gone, but if you shift it slowly or blip the throttle, it's okay.  Gotta fix that soon ($$$!!)||||reg||1
Z||000003||FIEROCIOUS||02-15-2000||06:53 AM||||I've got the same problem my car only has 50,000 miles on it. I think it's normal Fiero stuff. I drove my fathers S-10 the other day and when you shift at the nob it feels smooth. The gear shift is a foot+ off the floor and takes approx 6-8 inches to go from one gear to the other. But when I grabed down low approx 5 inches from the floor it feels EXACTLY like the Fiero "notchy"<BR>It's normal.<BR>I have the Muncie Getrag.<BR>What tranny has the weak 3rd?<BR>I've never heard about a weak 3rd syncro in the muncie! Although a friend ran his muncie without oil for six months and lost 5th. But thats it! All other gears were fine!<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||fiero56||02-15-2000||09:42 AM||||The muncie is the v-6 4-speed. The getrag is the v-6 5-speed.<BR>I think they are referring to the 5-speed.||||reg||1
Z||000005||BBBAD GT||02-15-2000||09:47 AM||||My 5 speed (87 GT) catches a little on the 2 to 3 shift.  Its not that bad, but enough to be noticed.  I can't say it does it all the time, but it is there.  I got 85k miles.  I'm not touching a thing unless it gets really bad, from reading your post.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000006||theogre||02-15-2000||12:12 PM||||Could be syncro problems or the detent pin(s) worn/binding. These spring loaded pins hold the shifter in gear. They are inside the tranny. <P>In some cases they are externally acessable by removing a plug. I don't know if they are so on the Fiero trannys.||||reg||1
Z||000007||fiero56||02-15-2000||02:36 PM||||Could the pins be the reason the shifter doesn't slide through the gears real easily? When shifting, if I slowly pull the shifter out of gear to shift to another, it doesn't pull out of gear smoothly. Not notchy, but not a real fluid feel.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Alex4mula||02-15-2000||02:55 PM||||My 88 Formula catches a little going into 3rd only in the morning (cold starts). Once it warms up it works OK. I installed the Getrag Selector Arm Rebuild Kit from Rodney Dickman and it definitely improved that problem and also the 1st gear shifting problem I had. Getting into 1st has allways been problematic but now is better. Guess that synchro is bad. Anyway, Rodney's kit helps reduce clearances in the shifting mechanism making it more accurate. I recommend it and it is only $12.50.||||reg||1
Z||000009||fiero56||02-15-2000||03:36 PM||||I have been planning to buy the rebuild kit from Rodney for some time. Just never got around to it. Guess I should try, wouldn't hurt and its only $12. <BR>I have trouble getting it into first gear too. Not all the time, but I have to be almost at a standstill before the shifter will go in gear, and occasionally it won't go into first, I have to throw it into a couple of other gears first, then it will go into first. This tranny has never been abused, and I'd say 90% of the 150K miles are highway.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Alex4mula||02-15-2000||04:14 PM||||Fiero56, That is exactly what happens to me and exactly what I do when it happens. My car has 156K miles and I exchenged the tranny once. By 90K my old tranny broke the differential bearings. The old and the "new" (from jyard) one did the same. I learned to live with it. But with the kit it feels a little bit better. Only 2 days with it. Will know better in a week or so.||||reg||1
Z||000011||GWMORGAN||02-15-2000||11:43 PM||||Can someone please post the web address to Rodney Dickman's web site. Thanx.||||reg||1
